# 2026-08-22 — Removed lines 178-180 (`.env`, `.env.*`, `*.env`) which
# had been re-added despite the explicit warning at line 163-170. This
# is the third recurrence of this deployment blocker — Emergent's
# MANAGE_SECRETS → pull_source step fails with "read env file
# backend/.env: no such file or directory" when these patterns are
# present. DO NOT re-add them.
#
# 2026-08-23 — 4th recurrence removed. If you see `.env` / `.env.*` /
# `*.env` in this file again, do NOT edit around them — DELETE them.
# The pre-deploy sentinel at scripts/env_gitignore_sentinel.py
# will now fail the deploy loudly if they reappear.
#
# 2026-08-23 (post-deploy) — 5TH RECURRENCE. Something in Emergent's
# deploy pipeline is silently rewriting this file on disk to re-add
# `.env`, `.env.*`, `*.env` at the end IMMEDIATELY AFTER the deploy
# auto-commit succeeds. Git HEAD is fine (the auto-commit that
# includes our removal is committed); the offending lines only come
# back on the pod's working tree. Suspect: `emergent-preview-sync` or
# similar background tool. This needs Emergent Support to fix upstream.
#
# 2026-08-24 — 6TH RECURRENCE. Support ticket escalated to senior
# team; recurrence still happened on THIS deploy (bundle 7eac4931 →
# 3932ea74). Confirms the pipeline bug is 100% reproducible on every
# deploy from this pod. Sentinel caught it within seconds again.
#
# 2026-08-24 (email from Akhil @ Emergent Support): CONFIRMED
# platform-side.  A git tool that authors the "Auto-generated changes"
# commits is appending these three lines, and it recurs on pod
# create/resume.  Reproduced live on our environment, escalated to
# owning engineering team.  IMPORTANT correction to our runbook:
# the deploy pipeline itself does NOT read .gitignore, so these lines
# alone don't break the current deploy.  What DOES break the next
# deploy is any git-reset or checkout that runs after the corruption —
# it physically deletes backend/.env from the working tree, and THEN
# MANAGE_SECRETS → pull_source fails with "read env file backend/.env:
# no such file or directory".  Recurrence #2 (the history-reset kill)
# was this exact chain.  Our sentinel catches the corruption BEFORE
# any git op can act on it — Akhil confirmed it's "precisely the right
# shape".  Keep the sentinel in place until the platform fix lands.
#
# 2026-08-24 (afternoon) — 7TH RECURRENCE detected during pre-deploy
# audit.  Reply email to Akhil already includes Recurrence #6
# evidence; if 7+ recurrences accumulate before their fix lands we
# can send a follow-up.  Sentinel + auto-fix is holding.
#
# 2026-08-24 (post-deploy 8th) — 8TH RECURRENCE.  Same 3 lines,
# same post-deploy timing (within seconds of bundle 5181527b →
# 36fa46d3 going live).  We have plenty of evidence for Akhil's
# team; not sending a fresh follow-up unless the recurrence pattern
# changes (e.g. lines appear MID-deploy instead of post-deploy).
#
# 2026-08-24 (post-deploy 9th) — 9TH RECURRENCE.  Bundle 36fa46d3 →
# d130e52c.  Pattern unchanged.  Auto-fix keeps holding.
